{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>YHWH Elohim.</b> Merciful in judgment." "<b>You have begun to show Your servant.</b> An opening — to stand and pray even though a decree had been issued. He said to Him: From You I learned this, for You said to me (Exodus 32) ״וְעַתָּה הַנִּיחָה לִּי״ — and was I holding onto You? Rather, to open an opening, that it depended on me to pray over them; so too I thought to do now (Sifrei)." "<b>Your greatness.</b> This is the attribute of Your goodness. And so it says (Numbers 14) ״וְעַתָּה יִגְדַּל נָא כֹּחַ HaShem״." "<b>And Your hand.</b> This is Your right hand, which is stretched out to all who enter the world." "<b>Mighty.</b> That You conquer the attribute of judgment with mercy, by force (Sifrei)." "<b>For who is El, etc.</b> You are not like a king of flesh and blood who has advisors and a sanhedrin that restrain his hand when he wishes to do kindness and override his own measures — You, there is none who can restrain Your hand if You forgive me and annul Your decree. And according to its plain sense: You have begun to show Your servant the war against Sihon and Og — as it is written (Deuteronomy 2) ״רְאֵה הַחִלֹּתִי תֵּת לְפָנֶיךָ״ — show me the war of the thirty-one kings."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:54.898587149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}